#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e612d4ba-b772-5f56-a031-fdfc05d63221" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type II Region Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b5831fb-253f-5678-9008-03061bccdd5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369254} {:answer/id #uuid "252743c2-344a-5b6e-ba45-83659ef951dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}4y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369255} {:answer/id #uuid "f82718fe-da50-5935-a375-90ef6023c77a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}2y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369256} {:answer/id #uuid "7236ee80-6187-5677-93b9-79807230706f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369257} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a7d74f-30c0-514b-8b4e-cde98dbfca73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}8{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "252743c2-344a-5b6e-ba45-83659ef951dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}4y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369255} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ce72215-0e23-50c4-9361-f4733c1185bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369253}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "88bac1aa-ae5d-5e83-b675-070a94eb234f" :question/math-academy-id "q-161555" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/assets/dcc7c78752700a17970da69c3809a8c621aaf23580ab0c3329335083858bd019.png)\n\nGiven that $R$ is the type II region shown above, \n${∭}_{R}2y\\,\\text{d}V=$" :question/worked-solution "For a type II region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $yz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type II region enclosed between the back surface $x={u}_{1}(y,z)=1$ and the front surface $x={u}_{2}(y,z)=3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/assets/339d4658909da42d55a836af93c7fda425bbe8d0ce17f246b73a4ca28cb9f380.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,1\\le x\\le 3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I *plane* region in the $yz$-plane with the upper curve\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9\\,⟺\\,z=\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/assets/879425adc3b1e78a7ea6a59740c9d8634ac13f62dea8eedc764bb5f1b07c92c2.png)\n\nHence, $D={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}2y\\,\\text{d}V & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}2y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}2y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}2y[x]_{x=1}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}4y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369259 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bd48398-cb9d-579f-b7f7-0f6be19172ce" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1621af89-4203-5168-a583-fa8455ad8ac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369261} {:answer/id #uuid "f4a5a0fd-8930-5f42-ac12-69fb5125df49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369262} {:answer/id #uuid "cb913b56-7e96-5548-b0ea-eff0b619ff4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369263} {:answer/id #uuid "dcf6f23a-1ece-59d4-8621-fe55f507ce50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369264} {:answer/id #uuid "83776c52-d151-5560-9203-2c54d7c582a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb913b56-7e96-5548-b0ea-eff0b619ff4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369263} :answer-field/id #uuid "b14ff575-7e1f-5027-93d2-26c078f19fab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369260}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "80658726-e97d-5aa4-afa4-7636348d90c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-161569" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{z}^{2}}^{4}xyz\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{z}^{2}}^{4}xyz\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}yz{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x={z}^{2}}^{x=4}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}yz(\\frac{16}{2}-\\frac{{z}^{4}}{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}8yz-\\frac{1}{2}y{z}^{5}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}8yz-\\frac{1}{2}y{z}^{5}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}8yz-\\frac{1}{2}y{z}^{5}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}4y[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=2}-\\frac{y}{12}[{z}^{6}]_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}4y(4-0)-\\frac{y}{12}(64-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}16y-\\frac{16}{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{32}{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}{[{y}^{2}]}_{y=-1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}(4-1) \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369266 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bd48398-cb9d-579f-b7f7-0f6be19172ce" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c56e27d5-6b4a-5922-b080-92287b037d2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369268} {:answer/id #uuid "ec66dba7-051b-562b-9e02-ea6bdc169bd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369269} {:answer/id #uuid "87511b1d-5626-5d55-bbe4-76ce3b975e17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369270} {:answer/id #uuid "7183420f-0b41-56e2-922b-166979386755" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369271} {:answer/id #uuid "07385650-5329-5772-8a25-cc46356e133e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c56e27d5-6b4a-5922-b080-92287b037d2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369268} :answer-field/id #uuid "636603f3-3932-53c3-b50e-79f34b4a1090" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369267}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b512e451-458c-5b38-8668-ad8df73b30a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161573" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{y}^{z}(y+z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le z\\le 3}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{y}^{z}(y+z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}(y+z)[x]_{x=y}^{x=z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y+z)(z-y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{3}{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}-{y}^{2}z]}_{z=y}^{z=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}(27-{y}^{3})-{y}^{2}(3-y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}9-\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}+{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}9-3{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[9y-{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{6}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =9-1+\\frac{1}{6}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{49}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369273 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90adf237-9627-55f1-8f90-8fbc4acf02fc" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type II Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "392257ee-708c-556c-bd7d-01c579cfcda8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369275} {:answer/id #uuid "afbbba88-8843-57ab-b5ed-0aac1f77c232" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369276} {:answer/id #uuid "052cd864-e1ec-539f-a0fb-0876bf7a862c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369277} {:answer/id #uuid "92951d3d-e30e-5f77-b567-a134b8e78310" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369278} {:answer/id #uuid "ccd921ba-c662-5efb-9078-24ad9a290e90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "052cd864-e1ec-539f-a0fb-0876bf7a862c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369277} :answer-field/id #uuid "f49f12e6-4c7c-5c51-8888-9be8600526ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369274}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5a66da8d-d90a-52b1-a62c-b67cb888dce1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161579" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}18x\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type II region given by \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le yz}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}18x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{yz}18x\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{yz}18x\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{yz}18x\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[9{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=yz}dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}9(yz)^{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}9{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}9{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}9{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[3{y}^{2}{z}^{3}]_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,dy & =[{y}^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369280 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e612d4ba-b772-5f56-a031-fdfc05d63221" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type II Region Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1539905c-31ca-5f9a-a5bb-41cccedbe770" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369282} {:answer/id #uuid "73ba9b16-7cd0-57e6-bd6a-27e7ac950640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369283} {:answer/id #uuid "3ed1078c-f0c3-5574-bfeb-9b2afb875942" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369284} {:answer/id #uuid "90ebb216-2253-5f8a-aabd-9a1329f9c471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369285} {:answer/id #uuid "f7934b77-808b-5f4f-a6ba-3a49428240a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ed1078c-f0c3-5574-bfeb-9b2afb875942" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369284} :answer-field/id #uuid "f450d0a3-205f-54c4-8ec5-d3a188c34f74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "033a0d68-da89-5d99-b52c-977f5ed7c12f" :question/math-academy-id "q-161782" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/assets/d148f8e38e2ad3bc7b1ca97a15b69c23ce315bc67ac2738009ca12f0fd7aef72.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{yz}{2}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/assets/ead71a275dfa4d4a0e07a02400e30f85440b3af8ca5a7f8d0cf0ebed60da8a6a.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 4-2y+3z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/assets/6e48e66eb003be316573e5b44948fcbce43b07e78fea97a7865ecf5eb4b4404a.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 4-2y+3z}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{yz}{2}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-2y+3z}\\frac{yz}{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-2y+3z}\\frac{yz}{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-2y+3z}\\frac{yz}{2}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{yz}{2}[x]_{x=0}^{x=4-2y+3z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{yz}{2}(4-2y+3z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}(4yz-2{y}^{2}z+3y{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}(4yz-2{y}^{2}z+3y{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}(4yz-2{y}^{2}z+3y{z}^{2})\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}{[2y{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(18y-9{y}^{2}+27y)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(45y-9{y}^{2})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(45y-9{y}^{2})\\,dy & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{45}{2}{y}^{2}-3{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(90-24)-0 \\\\  & =33.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
